WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.730
Hollywood movies have envisioned a future

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.580
of hoverboards and flying cars.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.683
These imaginary machines might
not be too far from reality.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.400
By 2030 a quarter of
shared passenger miles

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.630
traveled in America's roads could

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.793
be in self-driving vehicles.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.630
It's believe eight out of ten people

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:28.743
will be using Robo taxis in
cities where available by 2035.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.893
There will also be more
emphasis on sharing journeys.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.920
All this could reduce the number of cars

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.920
on city streets by 60%, emissions by 80%,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.463
and road accidents by 90%.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:50.670
And then there are flying cars.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.943
Or more accurately, passenger
drones and helicopter hybrids.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.683
Uber is investing heavily
in this technology.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.820
Los Angeles, Dallas, and
some states in Australia

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:06.363
could see test flights
within a couple of years.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.610
But these cross-city flights will require

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:12.410
changes to air traffic control systems.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.380
Which will probably take longer to develop

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.453
than the flying vehicles themselves.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.343
Traveling across country
could be far quicker too.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.763
China is leading the world
in high speed bullet trains,

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:30.083
that are capable of traveling
over 400 kilometers per hour.

00:01:31.881 --> 00:01:35.260
By 2020 80% of the country's major cities

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:36.810
could be linked to the network.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.770
But for high speed travel, the ambitious

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.183
Hyperloop could leave
bullet trains in the dust.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.710
It's an ambitious system in which pods

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.873
move along tubes in the near vacuum.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.850
The lack of air resistance means

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:57.830
pods could reach speeds of
over 1000 kilometers per hour.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.440
Virgin wants to deliver
a fully operational

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.963
Hyperloop system by the mid 2020's.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.260
The company claims it's Hyperloop pods

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:13.363
could travel from Los Angeles
to Las Vegas in 30 minutes.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.790
But the potential dangers of travel

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.330
at such great speeds and the cost

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.193
mean the Hyperloop will not
be a reality for decades.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.600
In the air the makers of supersonic jets

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.983
are promising to slash travel times too.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:35.690
Aerion wants to carry
12 passengers in luxury

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:38.073
at 1.4 times the speed of sound.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.903
About 60% faster than
typical aircraft today.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.670
And rival Boom hopes to be flying

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.533
its' supersonic airline by 2023.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:54.292
Carrying 55 passengers up to
2.2 times the speed of sound.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.873
Skeptics say these ideas are
impractical and expensive,

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.153
with many technical
challenges to overcome.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.630
Despite this tech and
engineering companies

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:11.560
are boldly taking up the
challenges of passenger transit.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.123
Promising to propel us into the future.

